<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.3.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01286</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.3.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>5315b4d2-39d4-4c50-8080-6c864de3f3b3</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise id="_47aa30b9-ab56-418a-b39c-4ec8704c046e" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Which expression equals \(2^7\)?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(2+2+2+2+2+2+2\)</para>
            <para>\(2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2\)</para>
            <para>\(2 \cdot 7\)</para>
            <para>\(2+7\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.3.4.
    </para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2\).
    </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="d4ae43a2-6c9d-4eb8-9bea-7160d3e0bea9" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>The graph shows the yearly balance, in dollars, of investment account A. The table shows the yearly balance, in dollars, of investment account B.</para>

          <para>(<media alt="Graph of a function on grid."><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_05_13_01.svg"/></media>)
          <table class="os-raise-skinnytable"><tgroup cols="2"><tbody><row><entry><emphasis>Number of years</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>Amount in dollars</emphasis></entry></row><row><entry>
                  0
                </entry><entry>
                  $2,000
                </entry></row><row><entry>
                  1
                </entry><entry>
                  $2,150
                </entry></row><row><entry>
                  2
                </entry><entry>
                  $2,300
                </entry></row><row><entry>
                  3
                </entry><entry>
                  $2,450
                </entry></row><row><entry>
                  4
                </entry><entry>
                  $2,600
                </entry></row></tbody></tgroup></table>
          
      </para>
            <para>Investment A is a/n:</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.3.3.
    </para>
            <para>The correct answer is investment A is an exponential function.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_2e8018d8-02b2-44d7-93ec-2d588f989d63" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Investment B is a/n:</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.3.3.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is investment B is a linear function.

    </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="fbad6471-c6ee-45b1-bc1d-256b4c9d53e3" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Which of the following statements are true? Select two that apply.</para>
            <para>The graph shows the yearly balance, in dollars, of investment account A. The table shows the yearly balance, in dollars, of investment account B.</para>

          <para>(<media alt="Graph of a function on grid."><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_05_13_02.svg"/></media>)
          <table class="os-raise-skinnytable"><tgroup cols="2"><tbody><row><entry><emphasis>Number of years</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>Amount in dollars</emphasis></entry></row><row><entry>
                  0
                </entry><entry>
                  $2,000
                </entry></row><row><entry>
                  1
                </entry><entry>
                  $2,150
                </entry></row><row><entry>
                  2
                </entry><entry>
                  $2,300
                </entry></row><row><entry>
                  3
                </entry><entry>
                  $2,450
                </entry></row><row><entry>
                  4
                </entry><entry>
                  $2,600
                </entry></row></tbody></tgroup></table>
          
      </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.3.2.
    </para>
            <para>The correct answers are “Investment A has a common ratio” and “Investment B is growing by the same number of dollars each year.”
    </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_5194cfd4-7a35-4cf5-8e07-a1591abd5323" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Investment account 1 starts with a balance of $200 and doubles every year. Investment account 2 starts with $1,000 and increases by $100 each year.  How long does it take for each account to double?</para>
            <para>How many years will it take investment account 1 to double?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.3.1.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is investment account 1 will double after 1 year.
    </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_612a528e-7954-4e6c-9072-ab22608e43cc" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>How many years will it take investment account 2 to double?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.3.1.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is investment account 2 will double after 10 years.
    </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_6b5c04b5-8090-4f89-a000-25b2f7d21a5a" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>A population of ants is 10,000 at the start of April. Since then, it triples each month. How many ants will there be 1 month later?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>10,003</para>
            <para>10,300</para>
            <para>30,000</para>
            <para>90,000</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.3.3.
    </para>
            <para>The correct answer is 30,000.
    </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="b2a066e0-6c5c-444e-bed3-c0ebd63e6c9a" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>A population of ants is 10,000 at the start of April. Since then, it triples each month. Which values complete the table?
          
          <table class="os-raise-skinnytable"><tgroup cols="2"><tbody><row><entry><emphasis>months since April</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>number of ants</emphasis></entry></row><row><entry>
                  0
                </entry><entry>
                  10,000
                </entry></row><row><entry>
                  1
                </entry><entry>
                  30,000
                </entry></row><row><entry>
                  2
                </entry><entry>
                   
                </entry></row><row><entry>
                  3
                </entry><entry>
                   
                </entry></row><row><entry>
                  4
                </entry><entry>
                   
                </entry></row></tbody></tgroup></table>
          
      </para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>50,000, 70,000, 90,000</para>
            <para>90,000, 270,000, 510,000</para>
            <para>40,000, 70,000, 110,000</para>
            <para>33,000, 33,300, 33,330</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.3.4.
    </para>
            <para>The correct answer is 90,000, 270,000, 510,000.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_7fc355fd-7699-488f-8921-1f1e256f30ac" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>A population of ants triples each month. If there are \(n\) ants in one month, which expression represents how many ants there will be one month later?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\( 3^n\)</para>
            <para>\( n^3\)</para>
            <para>\(3n\)</para>
            <para>\(n+3\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.3.4.
    </para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(3n\).
    </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_87c78b8b-26b8-41e3-8460-5a784a34a678" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>A swimming pool contains 500 gallons of water. A hose is turned on, and it fills the pool at a rate of 24 gallons per minute. Which expression represents the amount of water in the pool, in gallons, after 8 minutes?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(500 \cdot 24 \cdot 8\)</para>
            <para>\(500+24+8\)</para>
            <para>\(500+24 \cdot 8\)</para>
            <para>\(500\cdot 248\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.3.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(500+24 \cdot 8\).
    </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="e92fbc0f-e497-4ac1-a2d8-845e0aa31bd2" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>The population of a city is 100,000. It doubles each decade for 5 decades.<emphasis>Select the two</emphasis> expressions that represent the population of the city after 5 decades.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.3.4.
    </para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(100,000 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2\), \(100,000 \cdot 2^5\).
    </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="bc09b419-b906-4baa-a7fe-96fe89ca2aa1" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Bank account C starts with $10 and doubles each week. Bank account D starts with $1,000 and grows by $500 each week.      </para>
          <para>When will account C contain more money than account D?</para>

            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>Account C will contain more money than account D after 2 weeks.</para>
            <para>Account C will never contain more money than account D.</para>
            <para>Account C will contain more money than account D after 7 weeks.</para>
            <para>Account C will contain more money than account D after 10 weeks.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.3.3.
    </para>
            <para>The correct answer is account C will contain more money than account D after 10 weeks.
    </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>